  "tradeoff": "In general a central difference has O(\u03b5\u00b2) truncation error and roughly O(\u03b5_machine/\u03b5) cancellation error. This particular L(w1) = (8 w1 - 20)^2 is a quadratic, so the O(\u03b5\u00b2) term is identically zero and moderate \u03b5 (1e-2 \u2026 1e-6) recover 64 to nearly machine precision in float64. At \u03b5 \u2264 1e-12 the two nearby losses collide and cancellation dominates. float64 (\u03b5_machine \u2248 2e-16) is still required: the same sweep in float32 would start losing digits much earlier.",
